:name: RT1180 peripheral models — single load list
:description: Every C# peripheral this project ships, in dependency order.

# ⭐ ONE LIST, INCLUDED BY EVERY .resc AND BY THE ROBOT SUITE.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Each .resc used to carry its own hand-maintained list
# of 'i @peripherals/*.cs' lines. Adding a peripheral to a .repl then meant
# remembering to add its include to FIVE scripts plus the Robot suite, and
# forgetting one fails LOUDLY but only on the scripts you forgot -- the
# platform simply will not load.
#
# THAT MISTAKE HAPPENED THREE TIMES IN ONE SESSION: LPI2C/FXLS8974 (Robot),
# USB (Robot), and EMDIO -- where I updated rt1180_m1.resc only, and the six
# Tier A rows, which load the SAME m1.repl through rt1180_tierA.resc, all went
# from PASS/BANNER to FAIL. MEASURED: a full sweep read 22/29 instead of 27/29,
# and every lost row was Tier A. The score was wrong for a harness reason, not
# a model reason -- exactly the class this project keeps catching elsewhere.
#
# ORDER MATTERS: Renode compiles each file to its own assembly, so a model that
# references another must be loaded after it (CCM after Anadig; SAI after CCM
# and eDMA). This list preserves the order that was verified working.

i @/home/kyle/Documents/GitHub/rt1180renode/peripherals/IMXRT1180_eDMA4.cs
i @/home/kyle/Documents/GitHub/rt1180renode/peripherals/IMXRT1180_SRC.cs
